 \u003cbeth@brennie.ca\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2048762 - Use AboutRedirector for about:studies  a=diannaS DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314997\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316570\n", "files": ["browser/components/about/AboutRedirector.cpp", "browser/components/about/components.conf", "toolkit/components/normandy/ShieldContentProcess.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/normandy/components.conf", "toolkit/components/normandy/content/AboutPages.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/normandy/moz.build"], "git_node": "3e9e63dd4dbffba4a42d72172140126ae977ead7", "git_parents": ["b4c10225da66701c3ad9563dda7754f63690b1d6"], "node": "aff1ad6f20b424840b62fcee280503936646f4ce", "parents": ["60a7492440da69a63621df6cc551697380086eec"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785981591, "git_changesets": ["3e9e63dd4dbffba4a42d72172140126ae977ead7"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "208": {"changesets": [{"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060000. r=gfx-reviewers,nical, a=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315942\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/WebGLContextGL.cpp"], "git_node": "271ac54c67cca230656b3eeea9d1d2e0935b662c", "git_parents": ["3e9e63dd4dbffba4a42d72172140126ae977ead7"], "node": "b50ddc85fd17eb8e72922911c03acea77870e3be", "parents": ["aff1ad6f20b424840b62fcee280503936646f4ce"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785981723, "git_changesets": ["271ac54c67cca230656b3eeea9d1d2e0935b662c"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "209": {"changesets": [{"author": "Michael Kaply \u003cmozilla@kaply.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059825 - Use Cu.isInAutomation for enterprise policy test overrides.  a=diannaS DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315723\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316612\n", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/Policies.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/backgroundtasks/tests/BackgroundTask_policies.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/backgroundtasks/tests/browser/browser_xpcom_graph_wait.js", "toolkit/components/enterprisepolicies/EnterprisePoliciesParent.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "a4aab3178e8ae44990a6b063082d3a9f932e65cf", "git_parents": ["271ac54c67cca230656b3eeea9d1d2e0935b662c"], "node": "cb6c338117b08e30025abef1eb98c2f451739d14", "parents": ["b50ddc85fd17eb8e72922911c03acea77870e3be"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786022835, "git_changesets": ["a4aab3178e8ae44990a6b063082d3a9f932e65cf"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "21": {"changesets": [{"author": "Marco Bonardo \u003cmbonardo@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053482 - CopyFavicon should only copy across same-site pages.  a=diannaS DONTBUILD\n\n- Block non-http/https favicon copies in AsyncTryCopyFavicons; both source\n  and destination must use http or https.\n- Block cross-domain favicon copies using eTLD+1 comparison; falls back to\n  host for special schemes. Resolves false if eTLD service is unavailable.\n- Downgrade copyFavicons failure in TopSites from console.error to debug.\n- Mark TopSites-fetched icons as rich icons (isRich=true).\n- Adjust tests to use same-domain URIs for existing copy tests; add\n  cross-domain and non-http/https tests.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311126\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313463\n", "files": ["browser/components/topsites/TopSites.sys.mjs", "browser/components/topsites/test/unit/test_FaviconProvider.js", "toolkit/components/places/nsFaviconService.cpp", "toolkit/components/places/tests/favicons/test_copyFavicons.js"], "git_node": "7e0cfa96cb3b3511b11f8b5fe0377808db762646", "git_parents": ["115daaaad7907a05a409190d75651081ecd3058b"], "node": "0548714d912b5992654b510c8bbcd28bde728ba3", "parents": ["daa608d82bcd2cd7a87af5b723616038b20cc86a"], "tags": []}], "date": 1784742685, "git_changesets": ["7e0cfa96cb3b3511b11f8b5fe0377808db762646"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "210": {"changesets": [{"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059607 - Check for failed MapBufferRange in GetBufferSubData.  a=diannaS DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315844\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316698\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/WebGL2ContextBuffers.cpp"], "git_node": "623e1c3cc6f6ac32b1eb5c4474ef0ab5f875358c", "git_parents": ["a4aab3178e8ae44990a6b063082d3a9f932e65cf"], "node": "9f2e319bd2c7139f47667b9f871b6f2f481db4c8", "parents": ["cb6c338117b08e30025abef1eb98c2f451739d14"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786022857, "git_changesets": ["623e1c3cc6f6ac32b1eb5c4474ef0ab5f875358c"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "211": {"changesets": [{"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053579 - avoid DescendingSeqNumComp\u003cuint16_t\u003e as comparator in std::set.  a=diannaS DONTBUILD\n\nThis is a combined cherry-pick of upstream libwebrtc bf6f744d19, 5ecea90550,\n6395da1ed7.\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/bf6f744d19a84a7d0c3f5acbc844123a8197165a\n       Check RTP sequence number order when assembling H264 frame in PacketBuffer\n\n       PacketBuffer::buffer_ slots can be re-used by packets with with\n       different sequence numbers when their difference is multiple of\n       buffer_.size()\n\n       Non-H264 code path validates RTP sequence numbers continuity in\n       `PotentialNewFrame` helper, H264 code path missed such check as the new\n       test demonstrate.\n\n       Bug: chromium:537233963\n       Change-Id: I6af0f52bfcb3a4437450dffcece85bee7ce172cd\n       Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/490840\n       Reviewed-by: \u00c5sa Persson \u003casapersson@webrtc.org\u003e\n       Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n       Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48222}\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/5ecea90550816628fa124e7cf55f4cdbc5aa4a7e\n       In PacketBuffer use helper to find packet slot in the buffer\n\n       This is a preparation for using unwrapped int64_t instead of wrapped\n       uint16_t RTP sequence number in PacketBuffer. Using modular works when\n       sequence number is unsigned but produces incorrect result when signed\n       sequence number happens to be negative.\n\n       Bug: chromium:537233963\n       Change-Id: I515cb7441d052a2823eee4891bb4e17b254d602f\n       Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/491920\n       Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n       Reviewed-by: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n       Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48231}\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/6395da1ed7da9f3a8d97475c4e8db722d9415e6f\n       Use unwrappred RTP sequence numbers in PacketBuffer\n\n       Thus avoid brittle DescendingSeqNumComp\u003cuint16_t\u003e as comparator in set.\n       Such comparator lacks some properties like transitivity making it\n       dangerous to use with the std::set\n\n       Bug: chromium:537233963\n       Change-Id: I400b423ab3f0d557219d459752e00d211fd97450\n       Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/491041\n       Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n       Reviewed-by: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n       Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48232}\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316661\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/api/video/rtp_video_frame_assembler.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/packet_buffer.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/packet_buffer.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/packet_buffer_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/rtp_video_stream_receiver2.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/rtp_video_stream_receiver2.h"], "git_node": "8a74dd6c25d7dde7f458c832782964b8afade178", "git_parents": ["623e1c3cc6f6ac32b1eb5c4474ef0ab5f875358c"], "node": "bc471c2994a96f4973f3124fdaa6d0220ff7e692", "parents": ["9f2e319bd2c7139f47667b9f871b6f2f481db4c8"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786022878, "git_changesets": ["8a74dd6c25d7dde7f458c832782964b8afade178"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "212": {"changesets": [{"author": "Edgar Chen \u003cechen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054740 - Harden image transferable buffer size validation;  a=diannaS\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316444\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsContentUtils.cpp", "gfx/2d/DataSurfaceHelpers.cpp"], "git_node": "8a3a62a22075546eebb8410d4fe3ba29b200a521", "git_parents": ["8a74dd6c25d7dde7f458c832782964b8afade178"], "node": "2378816681b4fa2f2fe242488cddf5c229fba006", "parents": ["bc471c2994a96f4973f3124fdaa6d0220ff7e692"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060106.  a=diannaS\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316445\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsContentUtils.cpp"], "git_node": "7ea595b722277865e14732d148f47e09f3897b16", "git_parents": ["8a3a62a22075546eebb8410d4fe3ba29b200a521"], "node": "dc886f610b5d81d5f5301fc25a6c3da25d16f77a", "parents": ["2378816681b4fa2f2fe242488cddf5c229fba006"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786022900, "git_changesets": ["8a3a62a22075546eebb8410d4fe3ba29b200a521", "7ea595b722277865e14732d148f47e09f3897b16"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "213": {"changesets": [{"author": "Daisuke Akatsuka \u003cdaisuke@birchill.co.jp\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2035512 - Increase the urlbar input's line-height so the caret can be placed anywhere  a=diannaS DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313373\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316729\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/urlbar-searchbar.css"], "git_node": "3fa8daaff65b1204f1a134a34c54ccc37eea3b8a", "git_parents": ["7ea595b722277865e14732d148f47e09f3897b16"], "node": "87af08a4401aee1aeab4e55c81d42a534e190ca1", "parents": ["dc886f610b5d81d5f5301fc25a6c3da25d16f77a"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786046923, "git_changesets": ["3fa8daaff65b1204f1a134a34c54ccc37eea3b8a"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "214": {"changesets": [{"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060245.  a=diannaS DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316179\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316647\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/ipc/CanvasChild.cpp"], "git_node": "4f89ce61ac517ebb88fb1f44b302473e0283fc06", "git_parents": ["3fa8daaff65b1204f1a134a34c54ccc37eea3b8a"], "node": "44bead448c9116ee2d51e4da9effffe569d07776", "parents": ["87af08a4401aee1aeab4e55c81d42a534e190ca1"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786046954, "git_changesets": ["4f89ce61ac517ebb88fb1f44b302473e0283fc06"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "215": {"changesets": [{"author": "Tom Schuster \u003ctschuster@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050536.  a=diannaS\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310030\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316814\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/ProcessIsolation.cpp", "dom/ipc/gtest/ProcessIsolationTest.cpp", "dom/workers/test/browser.toml", "dom/workers/test/browser_privilegedmozilla_remoteworker.js", "dom/workers/test/browser_serviceworker_fetch_new_process.js", "dom/workers/test/file_service_worker.js", "dom/workers/test/file_service_worker_container.html"], "git_node": "96204be9bdb719faf4051e4cd7cb7b3270912652", "git_parents": ["4f89ce61ac517ebb88fb1f44b302473e0283fc06"], "node": "7ebf8c94da4c873df991bb35e92781828f7738e2", "parents": ["44bead448c9116ee2d51e4da9effffe569d07776"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786047118, "git_changesets": ["96204be9bdb719faf4051e4cd7cb7b3270912652"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "216": {"changesets": [{"author": "Dianna Smith \u003cdsmith@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2035512 - Increase the urlbar input's line-height so the caret can be placed anywhere\" for causing bc failures a=backout\n\nThis reverts commit 3fa8daaff65b1204f1a134a34c54ccc37eea3b8a.\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/urlbar-searchbar.css"], "git_node": "7c1157df19d364d1c61221f7bd06f28a9059e305", "git_parents": ["96204be9bdb719faf4051e4cd7cb7b3270912652"], "node": "33a1ed95bfe6be094ce945aa02cafe3bd6ec5dca", "parents": ["7ebf8c94da4c873df991bb35e92781828f7738e2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dianna Smith \u003cdsmith@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2059825 - Use Cu.isInAutomation for enterprise policy test overrides.\" for causing linting failures a=backout\n\nThis reverts commit a4aab3178e8ae44990a6b063082d3a9f932e65cf.\n", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/Policies.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/backgroundtasks/tests/BackgroundTask_policies.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/backgroundtasks/tests/browser/browser_xpcom_graph_wait.js", "toolkit/components/enterprisepolicies/EnterprisePoliciesParent.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "3c115ee0efbb80dbe6b283f29402228045805ec0", "git_parents": ["7c1157df19d364d1c61221f7bd06f28a9059e305"], "node": "20d893c13963c0f4f8d1ff222a0a0bce0d2d4a75", "parents": ["33a1ed95bfe6be094ce945aa02cafe3bd6ec5dca"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786060243, "git_changesets": ["7c1157df19d364d1c61221f7bd06f28a9059e305", "3c115ee0efbb80dbe6b283f29402228045805ec0"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "217": {"changesets": [{"author": "Eitan Isaacson \u003ceitan@monotonous.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055347 - Checked if accessible expired in accessibilityCustomActions. r=morgan, a=dsmith DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312403\n", "files": ["accessible/mac/MOXAccessibleBase.mm"], "git_node": "2412a9145f32cdf4440553b77a4e2da47245ab86", "git_parents": ["3c115ee0efbb80dbe6b283f29402228045805ec0"], "node": "51e5b304cfbb400a6601ab278787fd860b6bed16", "parents": ["20d893c13963c0f4f8d1ff222a0a0bce0d2d4a75"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786068082, "git_changesets": ["2412a9145f32cdf4440553b77a4e2da47245ab86"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "218": {"changesets": [{"author": "Stephen A Pohl \u003cspohl@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051788: Clamp content-initiated window resizes to the screen in the parent process.  a=diannaS DONTBUILD\n\nBrowserParent::RecvSetDimensions() rescaled a resize request coming from content for DPI and passed it on without bounding the size, and nothing further down keeps a window near the size of its screen. The size passed to window.open() is already bounded that way in nsWindowWatcher::SizeOpenedWindow().\n\nThe size is now clamped to twice the available area of the screen the window is on. Twice rather than exactly the screen, because the size we get for a screen is not always accurate, on Wayland in particular, and all we need is to keep the size in a range the window can be given. The clamp lives in RecvSetDimensions() rather than in nsGlobalWindowOuter, because for a content window the resize is requested in the content process but carried out in the parent, so this is where it can be enforced.\n\nResizeByOuter() also added the deltas coming from content to the current size in 32-bit arithmetic, which overflows for large values. It now adds in 64 bits and keeps the result in range.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316180\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316942\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/popups/browser.toml", "browser/base/content/test/popups/browser_popup_resize_clamp.js", "dom/base/nsGlobalWindowOuter.cpp", "dom/ipc/BrowserParent.cpp"], "git_node": "71f56ab50cc42314104c531301fe7a9b26c718ff", "git_parents": ["2412a9145f32cdf4440553b77a4e2da47245ab86"], "node": "df4a5786150105cb7f16baf2439fbcc409c2e2f0", "parents": ["51e5b304cfbb400a6601ab278787fd860b6bed16"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786068648, "git_changesets": ["71f56ab50cc42314104c531301fe7a9b26c718ff"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "219": {"changesets": [{"author": "Julien Pages \u003cjpages@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056781 - wasm: Refactor interaction between debugger and continuations.  a=diannaS DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314770\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316927\n", "files": ["js/src/debugger/Debugger.cpp", "js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/js-promise-integration/debug-stale-cont-env.js", "js/src/vm/EnvironmentObject.cpp", "js/src/vm/EnvironmentObject.h"], "git_node": "2755d7ebfd5364b7851e59843e5ad988a89798dc", "git_parents": ["71f56ab50cc42314104c531301fe7a9b26c718ff"], "node": "c80eebf213b375e1ea3c32680ccf4aa0a56e42db", "parents": ["df4a5786150105cb7f16baf2439fbcc409c2e2f0"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786068674, "git_changesets": ["2755d7ebfd5364b7851e59843e5ad988a89798dc"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "22": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jens Stutte \u003cjstutte@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2046040 - Process the main thread event queue at least once before dooming it at shutdown.  a=diannaS DONTBUILD\n\nnsThreadManager::ShutdownMainThread() drains the main thread's event queue and then dooms it, so that nothing can be queued once the main thread stops processing events. The drain loop checked for an empty queue first and only processed events when something was pending, so when the queue happened to be empty on entry it doomed immediately, without a final pass.\n\nThat final pass matters: processing runs a microtask checkpoint, and a checkpoint can settle promises and dispatch follow-up runnables - in particular the unhandled-rejection notification that AfterProcessMicrotasks queues for promises rejected without a handler. A promise can be rejected during the XPCOMShutdownFinal phase (e.g. when a ClearOnShutdown handler tears down an object that settles a pending promise) with no checkpoint having run since. If the queue is then empty when ShutdownMainThread() runs, the old loop doomed it without a checkpoint and the notification was never dispatched; the promises it would have held were only released when the cycle-collected context was torn down, after nsCycleCollector_shutdown(), tripping the \"Cycle collected object used on a thread without a cycle collector\" diagnostic assertion.\n\nRewrite the loop as a do/while so it always processes at least once before checking for an empty queue. The final pass runs a checkpoint that dispatches any pending notification while the main thread still processes events and the cycle collector is alive; the loop then delivers it before dooming the queue. This makes the \"queue empty on entry\" path behave like the \"queue non-empty\" path that already runs a checkpoint today.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312384\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313526\n", "files": ["xpcom/threads/nsThreadManager.cpp"], "git_node": "d71e0707af56fcb2dcb1b7ef214d3f8b65d45628", "git_parents": ["7e0cfa96cb3b3511b11f8b5fe0377808db762646"], "node": "582a2b44305a16093700466a659c375dbc7319e4", "parents": ["0548714d912b5992654b510c8bbcd28bde728ba3"], "tags": []}], "date": 1784742718, "git_changesets": ["d71e0707af56fcb2dcb1b7ef214d3f8b65d45628"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "220": {"changesets": [{"author": "John M. Schanck \u003cjschanck@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056509 - upgrade Firefox 153 to nss-rs 0.13.4. r=kershaw a=diannaS\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315378\n", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "netwerk/test/http3server/moz.build", "third_party/rust/nss-rs/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/nss-rs/.deny.toml", "third_party/rust/nss-rs/.github/CODEOWNERS", "third_party/rust/nss-rs/.github/actionlint.yml", "third_party/rust/nss-rs/.github/actions/check-android/action.yml", "third_party/rust/nss-rs/.github/actions/check-vm/action.yml", "third_party/rust/nss-rs/.github/dependabot.yml", "third_party/rust/nss-rs/.github/semantic.yml", "third_party/rust/nss-rs/.github/workflows/actionlint.yml", "third_party/rust/nss-rs/.github/workflows/check.yml", "third_party/rust/nss-rs/.github/workflows/claude.yml", "third_party/rust/nss-rs/.github/workflows/clippy.yml", "third_party/rust/nss-rs/.github/workflows/deny.yml", "third_party/rust/nss-rs/.github/workflows/dependency-review.yml", "third_party/rust/nss-rs/.github/workflows/firefox.yml", "third_party/rust/nss-rs/.github/workflows/machete.yml", "third_party/rust/nss-rs/.github/workflows/mutants.yml", "third_party/rust/nss-rs/.github/workflows/rustfmt.yml", "third_party/rust/nss-rs/.github/workflows/sanitize.yml", "third_party/rust/nss-rs/.github/workflows/sbom.yml", "third_party/rust/nss-rs/.github/workflows/semver.yml", "third_party/rust/nss-rs/Cargo.lock", "third_party/rust/nss-rs/Cargo.toml", "third_party/rust/nss-rs/bindings/bindings.toml", "third_party/rust/nss-rs/bindings/nspr_lib.h", "third_party/rust/nss-rs/build.rs", "third_party/rust/nss-rs/src/der.rs", "third_party/rust/nss-rs/src/freebl/mod.rs", "third_party/rust/nss-rs/src/lib.rs", "third_party/rust/nss-rs/tests/init.rs", "toolkit/library/moz.build"], "git_node": "7d0798bd91b376831559c3567736ccce79e0ce28", "git_parents": ["2755d7ebfd5364b7851e59843e5ad988a89798dc"], "node": "6cfff632bab2ceeaa5f6ece75f82d3425c100b83", "parents": ["c80eebf213b375e1ea3c32680ccf4aa0a56e42db"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786068834, "git_changesets": ["7d0798bd91b376831559c3567736ccce79e0ce28"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "221": {"changesets": [{"author": "Pascal Chevrel \u003cpascal@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2056134 - Part 5: