.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058110 - Don't queue picture task if pictureness hasn't changed.  a=diannaS DONTBUILD\n\nMatches the UnbindFromTree handling. I have another fix on top which is\na bit more annoying to test, but the test here should cover the broken\nwebsite.\n\nWithout this relevant-mutations.html fails the picture tests.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314436\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314892\n", "files": ["dom/html/HTMLImageElement.cpp", "dom/html/HTMLImageElement.h", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-img-element/support/relevant-mutations.js"], "git_node": "81a2c2bf12b924261ffd74ca235e3a0561b945c3", "git_parents": ["d8a1d3b6bd4f4de676a3310f959e9fa42727bbf8"], "node": "caf65490a92b32fdb6f76f03d963eecfbf01bd6b", "parents": ["fb65f765cc8264e712f885e0e4242e6ce567b3c9"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785412096, "git_changesets": ["81a2c2bf12b924261ffd74ca235e3a0561b945c3"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "81": {"changesets": [{"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058134 - Use HasAuthorSpecifiedBorderBackground() rather than background alpha.  a=diannaS\n\nThis matches what we do for ::target-text. This shouldn't regress\nbug 2043232 (which uses background-color: revert) because that doesn't\ncount as author-specified.\n\nWe couldn't do this when I wrote the regressing bug because of the\nborder-radius support that nova had, but that has been reverted since.\nArguably, we should split the border-background bit, maybe...\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314607\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314890\n", "files": ["layout/generic/nsTextPaintStyle.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/selection-background-color-revert-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/selection-background-color-revert.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/selection-background-color-transparent-notref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/selection-background-color-transparent.html"], "git_node": "1f96bf63896a4ccd19c63e9942b10a297437aaea", "git_parents": ["81a2c2bf12b924261ffd74ca235e3a0561b945c3"], "node": "284b4d9af9f6469a8b4eb6f1ed03060dcb3488f1", "parents": ["caf65490a92b32fdb6f76f03d963eecfbf01bd6b"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785412559, "git_changesets": ["1f96bf63896a4ccd19c63e9942b10a297437aaea"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "82": {"changesets": [{"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2045721: Add IPCClientInfo type checking  a=diannaS DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D305382\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314870\n", "files": ["dom/clients/manager/ClientManagerParent.cpp", "dom/clients/manager/moz.build", "dom/fetch/FetchParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.cpp", "dom/serviceworkers/ServiceWorkerContainerParent.cpp", "ipc/glue/BackgroundParentImpl.cpp"], "git_node": "cd4122a8793f9425594decda4c9a038d604b0a32", "git_parents": ["1f96bf63896a4ccd19c63e9942b10a297437aaea"], "node": "cfc5f95dbccd14028cd2b33946b96ed28adc5c93", "parents": ["284b4d9af9f6469a8b4eb6f1ed03060dcb3488f1"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785415583, "git_changesets": ["cd4122a8793f9425594decda4c9a038d604b0a32"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "83": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jon Coppeard \u003cjcoppeard@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053337 - Part 1: Always add ephemeron edge for symbol keyed weak map entries  a=diannaS DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311573\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315250\n", "files": ["js/src/gc/Marking.cpp", "js/src/gc/WeakMap.cpp"], "git_node": "b3865cba263c98d5a7b5857c1028b548e8860397", "git_parents": ["cd4122a8793f9425594decda4c9a038d604b0a32"], "node": "673264a98847363440cd4fc843487ab891467041", "parents": ["cfc5f95dbccd14028cd2b33946b96ed28adc5c93"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785415606, "git_changesets": ["b3865cba263c98d5a7b5857c1028b548e8860397"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "84": {"changesets": [{"author": "Ben Visness \u003cbvisness@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051555: In case of OOM, make an inline array.  a=diannaS DONTBUILD\n\nFor both array and struct objects, an OOM can occur in between\nallocating the object and allocating its out-of-line data area. For\nstructs we don't really have a choice but to be aware of null data\npointers in obj_trace and obj_moved, but for arrays we can just convert\nthe failed array into an empty inline-storage array.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311827\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314972\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/gc/bug2051555.js", "js/src/wasm/WasmGcObject-inl.h", "js/src/wasm/WasmGcObject.cpp"], "git_node": "8467a1435edab9f0bd30798cd2f4fba5fcda4d9a", "git_parents": ["b3865cba263c98d5a7b5857c1028b548e8860397"], "node": "8a707c77c07c4c8e8086f41c9416100b7d7f010a", "parents": ["673264a98847363440cd4fc843487ab891467041"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785415631, "git_changesets": ["8467a1435edab9f0bd30798cd2f4fba5fcda4d9a"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "85": {"changesets": [{"author": "Alastor Wu \u003calwu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2045380 - Validate input video frame dimensions before conversion in the encoder path.  a=diannaS\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314490\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315009\n", "files": ["dom/media/ImageConversion.cpp", "dom/media/ImageConversion.h", "dom/media/ipc/RemoteMediaDataEncoderParent.cpp"], "git_node": "fb043201b463f5e23f40574922108e40967a500a", "git_parents": ["8467a1435edab9f0bd30798cd2f4fba5fcda4d9a"], "node": "aeec7d8aaa687dbf8c5e831040673c0eba8598e3", "parents": ["8a707c77c07c4c8e8086f41c9416100b7d7f010a"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785415656, "git_changesets": ["fb043201b463f5e23f40574922108e40967a500a"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "86": {"changesets": [{"author": "Kershaw Chang \u003ckershaw@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050482 - Filter ServiceWorker cookiechange events,  a=diannaS\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312963\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315276\n", "files": ["dom/cookiestore/CookieStoreNotifier.cpp", "dom/cookiestore/CookieStoreParent.cpp", "dom/cookiestore/CookieStoreSubscriptionService.cpp"], "git_node": "dc590afb7c294cbe67ac4e72c2824d3e9cc33c1c", "git_parents": ["fb043201b463f5e23f40574922108e40967a500a"], "node": "c795b0c1a6e5490e3ffc15f4384da1b03764a024", "parents": ["aeec7d8aaa687dbf8c5e831040673c0eba8598e3"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785436968, "git_changesets": ["dc590afb7c294cbe67ac4e72c2824d3e9cc33c1c"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "87": {"changesets": [{"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053757 - Tweak expectations of input-element-pseudo-open.optional.html.ini.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311404\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314229\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-pseudo/input-element-pseudo-open.optional.html.ini"], "git_node": "8cfe9709cd5a8ddcfdf042a22a8db87e08703c62", "git_parents": ["dc590afb7c294cbe67ac4e72c2824d3e9cc33c1c"], "node": "85d8ba0d233c98390c48750fb85072b75dc1f51e", "parents": ["c795b0c1a6e5490e3ffc15f4384da1b03764a024"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785453012, "git_changesets": ["8cfe9709cd5a8ddcfdf042a22a8db87e08703c62"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "88": {"changesets": [{"author": "scottdowne \u003csdowne@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056650 - Mark moz-newtab-wallpaper as known-cacheable so newtab custom wallpapers stop flashing a=pascalc DONTBUILD\n\nNewtab has its own special wallpaper protocol for custom wallpapers, and it\nwas missing from the knownCacheable detection. Combined with newtab\npreloading, that made the image periodically fail ValidateEntry and get\nre-requested, causing the flash.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313305\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314081\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsContentUtils.cpp"], "git_node": "ccad06cc85cb384fa24782021b3557ada8d91e72", "git_parents": ["8cfe9709cd5a8ddcfdf042a22a8db87e08703c62"], "node": "f771d1aa37adc8e973072263d227cfe0d40d8ba4", "parents": ["85d8ba0d233c98390c48750fb85072b75dc1f51e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056917 - [riscv64] Qualify enum BaseOpcode in return type position in InstructionBase. a=pascalc DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313478\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314269\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/riscv64/base/Instruction.h"], "git_node": "0a61723a4dbaef1b15fd7ba6e4d502c19b6fb0c7", "git_parents": ["ccad06cc85cb384fa24782021b3557ada8d91e72"], "node": "8b43d577a229b883c7a8d59509ae8abfcd9bbb6d", "parents": ["f771d1aa37adc8e973072263d227cfe0d40d8ba4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan-Erik Rediger \u003cjrediger@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053012 - Update anyhow, memmap2, crossbeam-epoch a=pascalc\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310988\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312441\n", "files": [".cargo/audit.toml", "Cargo.lock", "supply-chain/audits.toml", "supply-chain/imports.lock", "third_party/rust/anyhow/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/anyhow/.cargo_vcs_info.json", "third_party/rust/anyhow/.clippy.toml", "third_party/rust/anyhow/.github/FUNDING.yml", "third_party/rust/anyhow/.github/workflows/ci.yml", "third_party/rust/anyhow/Cargo.lock", "third_party/rust/anyhow/Cargo.toml", "third_party/rust/anyhow/Cargo.toml.orig", "third_party/rust/anyhow/README.md", "third_party/rust/anyhow/build.rs", "third_party/rust/anyhow/src/backtrace.rs", "third_party/rust/anyhow/src/chain.rs", "third_party/rust/anyhow/src/context.rs", "third_party/rust/anyhow/src/ensure.rs", "third_party/rust/anyhow/src/error.rs", "third_party/rust/anyhow/src/fmt.rs", "third_party/rust/anyhow/src/kind.rs", "third_party/rust/anyhow/src/lib.rs", "third_party/rust/anyhow/src/macros.rs", "third_party/rust/anyhow/src/nightly.rs", "third_party/rust/anyhow/src/ptr.rs", "third_party/rust/anyhow/src/wrapper.rs", "third_party/rust/anyhow/tests/compiletest.rs", "third_party/rust/anyhow/tests/test_autotrait.rs", "third_party/rust/anyhow/tests/test_backtrace.rs", "third_party/rust/anyhow/tests/test_context.rs", "third_party/rust/anyhow/tests/test_ensure.rs", "third_party/rust/anyhow/tests/test_ffi.rs", "third_party/rust/anyhow/tests/test_fmt.rs", "third_party/rust/anyhow/tests/test_macros.rs", "third_party/rust/anyhow/tests/test_repr.rs", "third_party/rust/anyhow/tests/ui/ensure-nonbool.rs", "third_party/rust/anyhow/tests/ui/ensure-nonbool.stderr", "third_party/rust/anyhow/tests/ui/must-use.stderr", "third_party/rust/anyhow/tests/ui/no-impl.stderr", "third_party/rust/anyhow/tests/ui/temporary-value.stderr", "third_party/rust/crossbeam-epoch/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/crossbeam-epoch/.cargo_vcs_info.json", "third_party/rust/crossbeam-epoch/CHANGELOG.md", "third_party/rust/crossbeam-epoch/Cargo.lock", "third_party/rust/crossbeam-epoch/Cargo.toml", "third_party/rust/crossbeam-epoch/Cargo.toml.orig", "third_party/rust/crossbeam-epoch/README.md", "third_party/rust/crossbeam-epoch/build-common.rs", "third_party/rust/crossbeam-epoch/build.rs", "third_party/rust/crossbeam-epoch/no_atomic.rs", "third_party/rust/crossbeam-epoch/src/atomic.rs", "third_party/rust/crossbeam-epoch/src/collector.rs", "third_party/rust/crossbeam-epoch/src/default.rs", "third_party/rust/crossbeam-epoch/src/deferred.rs", "third_party/rust/crossbeam-epoch/src/epoch.rs", "third_party/rust/crossbeam-epoch/src/guard.rs", "third_party/rust/crossbeam-epoch/src/internal.rs", "third_party/rust/crossbeam-epoch/src/lib.rs", "third_party/rust/crossbeam-epoch/src/sync/list.rs", "third_party/rust/crossbeam-epoch/src/sync/once_lock.rs", "third_party/rust/crossbeam-epoch/src/sync/queue.rs", "third_party/rust/memmap2/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/memmap2/.cargo_vcs_info.json", "third_party/rust/memmap2/.github/workflows/main.yml", "third_party/rust/memmap2/CHANGELOG.md", "third_party/rust/memmap2/Cargo.lock", "third_party/rust/memmap2/Cargo.toml", "third_party/rust/memmap2/Cargo.toml.orig", "third_party/rust/memmap2/README.md", "third_party/rust/memmap2/examples/cat.rs", "third_party/rust/memmap2/src/advice.rs", "third_party/rust/memmap2/src/lib.rs", "third_party/rust/memmap2/src/stub.rs", "third_party/rust/memmap2/src/unix.rs", "third_party/rust/memmap2/src/windows.rs"], "git_node": "b7a08193c0a0288e523b635771165cc3a9175b00", "git_parents": ["0a61723a4dbaef1b15fd7ba6e4d502c19b6fb0c7"], "node": "bb77346c82a175e6825505d7be5534fb9ef99787", "parents": ["8b43d577a229b883c7a8d59509ae8abfcd9bbb6d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alastor Wu \u003calwu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053586 - Part 1: Gate the runtime muted content attribute fallback behind a Nightly-only pref. a=pascalc\n\nThe muted content attribute became a live fallback for the muted state in bug\n2037015, implementing the \"muted\" concept [1]. Adding the attribute at runtime\nto a connected media element now mutes the element.\n\nFirefox is currently the only engine that applies this at runtime, so sites that\nadd the attribute to an already-playing element and expect audible output go\nsilent. Gate that runtime fallback behind a new pref that is enabled only on\nNightly, so release channels keep the previous, cross-engine behavior until the\nchange is broadly interoperable.\n\nThe parser and cloning paths and the muted IDL setter are unaffected.\n\n[1] https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/media.html#concept-media-muted\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311387\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312085\n", "files": ["dom/media/mediaelement/HTMLMediaElement.cpp", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "6e4acacd8e8d22cb4d3df7a7f782dff075dc54c0", "git_parents": ["b7a08193c0a0288e523b635771165cc3a9175b00"], "node": "2284a5c454ab99ae686293bce1e2013b089792a6", "parents": ["bb77346c82a175e6825505d7be5534fb9ef99787"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alastor Wu \u003calwu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053586 - Part 2: Record how often the runtime muted content attribute mutes a connected media element. a=pascalc\n\nTo decide when the runtime muted content-attribute fallback can be enabled on\nrelease channels, measure how often pages actually rely on it.\n\nAdd a counter recorded whenever the muted content attribute is added at runtime\nto a connected element that would otherwise be audible, that is, one that has an\naudio track, is not already muted, and has a non-zero volume. Elements that\nwould not be affected are ignored.\n\nThe counter is recorded independently of the gating pref so the pattern is\nmeasured on every channel.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311388\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312086\n", "files": ["dom/media/mediaelement/HTMLMediaElement.cpp", "dom/media/mediaelement/HTMLMediaElement.h", "dom/media/metrics.yaml"], "git_node": "e92ff26b8781187cf4dd3639eaf53f8273a15f7f", "git_parents": ["6e4acacd8e8d22cb4d3df7a7f782dff075dc54c0"], "node": "ded6a6dc1f6576808358a9313fd4c46f0d22be20", "parents": ["2284a5c454ab99ae686293bce1e2013b089792a6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alastor Wu \u003calwu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053586 - Part 3: Enable the muted-state pref for tests that rely on the runtime muted content attribute. a=pascalc\n\ntest_defaultMuted.html and the muted / event_volumechange web-platform tests\nassert that adding the muted content attribute at runtime mutes the element.\n\nThat behavior is now off by default outside Nightly, so force the pref on for\nthose tests to keep them passing on every channel.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311389\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312087\n", "files": ["dom/media/test/test_defaultMuted.html", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/media-elements/event_volumechange.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/media-elements/user-interface/muted.html.ini"], "git_node": "792331ea27dea877e60b73793cd873ef3d122885", "git_parents": ["e92ff26b8781187cf4dd3639eaf53f8273a15f7f"], "node": "2303ed4d9a25b4dcc46187f38c652da10e2f68b1", "parents": ["ded6a6dc1f6576808358a9313fd4c46f0d22be20"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alastor Wu \u003calwu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053586 - Part 4: Enable the muted-state pref for the remaining test that relies on the runtime muted content attribute. a=pascalc\n\nPart 1 gated the runtime muted content attribute behind a Nightly-only\npref, and Part 3 forced that pref on for the tests that depend on it. The\ncss/selectors \":muted matches the content attribute default\" subtest was\nmissed and fails once the pref defaults off outside Nightly, as surfaced\nby the central-as-beta simulation.\n\nForce the pref on so the subtest keeps exercising the runtime fallback and\npasses on every channel. The test also re-lists the pseudo-classes pref\nfrom its directory metadata, which a per-test prefs list would otherwise\noverride.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312299\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312541\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/selectors/media/sound-state.html.ini"], "git_node": "5de2e9a71b86b6d06fb69dc783d1220ade79f2ee", "git_parents": ["792331ea27dea877e60b73793cd873ef3d122885"], "node": "219be844420e943fc922d52dc764c92fc646ef5a", "parents": ["2303ed4d9a25b4dcc46187f38c652da10e2f68b1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Duncan McIntosh \u003cdmcintosh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2043426 - Isolate error checks in telemetry.nsh. a=pascalc DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D303203\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312530\n", "files": ["browser/installer/windows/nsis/telemetry.nsh", "browser/installer/windows/nsis/test_telemetry.nsh"], "git_node": "7e2a6fb3c1e1671ffb0a305353062f21c70048ab", "git_parents": ["5de2e9a71b86b6d06fb69dc783d1220ade79f2ee"], "node": "082de2aa8d718f15a9ff793c1364a69f01f3850f", "parents": ["219be844420e943fc922d52dc764c92fc646ef5a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nika Layzell \u003cnika@thelayzells.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054428 - Correctly unwrap url for blob principals, a=pascalc\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311846\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312277\n", "files": ["caps/BasePrincipal.cpp", "caps/tests/unit/test_origin.js"], "git_node": "9858e564373aae703f07d1b0b7427b20e9b6e31d", "git_parents": ["7e2a6fb3c1e1671ffb0a305353062f21c70048ab"], "node": "4d0a51a14b552c536b4e9d676a769ed6b49352ef", "parents": ["082de2aa8d718f15a9ff793c1364a69f01f3850f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053363 - Make telemetry data for IME, GTK and DE lifetime: application. a=pascalc DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310995\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312395\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/metrics.yaml"], "git_node": "1ca64071792877e6ab741f4f05306018b5ba2102", "git_parents": ["9858e564373aae703f07d1b0b7427b20e9b6e31d"], "node": "85ef43f3523ceef38461bff69248baed96ca4d32", "parents": ["4d0a51a14b552c536b4e9d676a769ed6b49352ef"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandre Poirot \u003cpoirot.alex@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054525 - [devtools] Fix toggling pseudo element containers. a=pascalc\n\nThe usage of bind() was harcoding a unique possible toggle value for\npseudo container.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312291\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312473\n", "files": ["devtools/client/inspector/rules/rules.js", "devtools/client/inspector/rules/test/browser_rules_pseudo-element_01.js"], "git_node": "598a89d4019d99d3db418b3d266249273661edcb", "git_parents": ["1ca64071792877e6ab741f4f05306018b5ba2102"], "node": "eb8a508c9a679a293c3f291df5d344e9664f6026", "parents": ["85ef43f3523ceef38461bff69248baed96ca4d32"], "tags": []}, {"author": "mandysGit \u003cmcheang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053710 - Suppress the NEW label for app-provided engines overridden by Third Party Engine. a=pascalc DONTBUILD\n\nThe NEW label is unnecessary when an application-provided engine is overridden by an\nthird-party search engine, since the user explicitly installed the third-party engine.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311662\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313072\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-searchMode/browser.toml", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-searchMode/browser_searchModeSwitcher_newBadge.js", "toolkit/components/search/ConfigSearchEngine.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/search/tests/xpcshell/test_appProvided_engine.js"], "git_node": "a03c67d412a2ebc71cb53cf8412ff9a7ab9da1e1", "git_parents": ["598a89d4019d99d3db418b3d266249273661edcb"], "node": "2de6fa50f02a4a88f455af8da324d9e8a34733f4", "parents": ["eb8a508c9a679a293c3f291df5d344e9664f6026"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053867 - Do not reuse `IMEContentObserver` instance if observing editing host is changed a=pascalc DONTBUILD\n\nCurrently, we allow users to edit content in a nested editing host in\na focused editing host. In this case,\n`mRootEditableNodeOrTextControlElement` is the focused editing host and\n`mRootElement` is the nested editing host and `IMEContentObserver` sent\n`IME_NOTIFY_IME_OF_FOCUS` as in `mRootElement`.\n\nWhen the nested editing host is moved outside the focused editing host,\nthe DOM focus is not changed. Therefore, `IMEContentObserver` needs to\nobserve the focused editing host. So, from IME point of view, IME focus\nis now changed. I.e., `IMEContentObserver` should be recreated to notify\nIME of a `blur` and `focus`.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311764\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313131\n", "files": ["dom/events/IMEContentObserver.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/editing/crashtests/move-nested-editing-host-to-input.html"], "git_node": "5ce9f39260dbdebf04128553ac452679480d92f7", "git_parents": ["a03c67d412a2ebc71cb53cf8412ff9a7ab9da1e1"], "node": "2d310af4ad32d9afb833ac0c0e1303203c59567c", "parents": ["2de6fa50f02a4a88f455af8da324d9e8a34733f4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ashley Hale \u003cahale@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055054 - query HDR display information and show it in about:support a=pascalc\n\nThis also fixes a bug in initializing MaxContentLightLevel but we currently aren't using that value so it does not change observed behavior.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312205\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313067\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/DOMTypes.ipdlh", "gfx/thebes/DeviceManagerDx.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxPlatform.cpp", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/gecko/GeckoAppShell.java", "widget/Screen.cpp", "widget/Screen.h", "widget/ScreenManager.cpp", "widget/android/ScreenHelperAndroid.cpp", "widget/cocoa/ScreenHelperCocoa.mm", "widget/gtk/ScreenHelperGTK.cpp", "widget/headless/HeadlessScreenHelper.cpp", "widget/uikit/ScreenHelperUIKit.mm", "widget/windows/ScreenHelperWin.cpp"], "git_node": "e790cdc1d44d6ce361c21ca573bd490b36ea1ef2", "git_parents": ["5ce9f39260dbdebf04128553ac452679480d92f7"], "node": "5dc4ca956f9d5f82b9cc0b09f0f60e2ca97640d3", "parents": ["2d310af4ad32d9afb833ac0c0e1303203c59567c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056926 - Paper over bug 1681745 / bug 1941972. a=pascalc\n\nSee the comment for reasoning, and bug 1681745 + bug 1941972 for\ncontext.\n\nNot a fan in many ways, since this is likely to cause wrong rendering at\nbest, and random crashes later down the line at worst. But at least I\nadd the crash reporter annotation message, if we then crash later down\nthe line...\n\nTested manually by removing select.css from my objdir and using the\nnon-nightly codepath.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313486\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314217\n", "files": ["dom/base/Document.cpp", "dom/base/ShadowRoot.cpp", "layout/style/GlobalStyleSheetCache.cpp", "layout/style/GlobalStyleSheetCache.h"], "git_node": "3b24bd46da070d8593d07c6d24561edaaf289025", "git_parents": ["e790cdc1d44d6ce361c21ca573bd490b36ea1ef2"], "node": "0c8fc61d8bb82a98df442334c7d56c3fa61821cf", "parents": ["5dc4ca956f9d5f82b9cc0b09f0f60e2ca97640d3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057731 - Add telemetry for the global stylesheet cache not finding the expected stylesheet. a=pascalc\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314213\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314281\n", "files": ["layout/base/metrics.yaml", "layout/style/GlobalStyleSheetCache.cpp"], "git_node": "b312309a3cb713fad42e4efc4f084fbdb888d3f6", "git_parents": ["3b24bd46da070d8593d07c6d24561edaaf289025"], "node": "f07803e1aa588589f5130a79f43e835614d1d0bc", "parents": ["0c8fc61d8bb82a98df442334c7d56c3fa61821cf"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785453180, "git_changesets": ["ccad06cc85cb384fa24782021b3557ada8d91e72", "0a61723a4dbaef1b15fd7ba6e4d502c19b6fb0c7", "b7a08193c0a0288e523b635771165cc3a9175b00", "6e4acacd8e8d22cb4d3df7a7f782dff075dc54c0", "e92ff26b8781187cf4dd3639eaf53f8273a15f7f", "792331ea27dea877e60b73793cd873ef3d122885", "5de2e9a71b86b6d06fb69dc783d1220ade79f2ee", "7e2a6fb3c1e1671ffb0a305353062f21c70048ab", "9858e564373aae703f07d1b0b7427b20e9b6e31d", "1ca64071792877e6ab741f4f05306018b5ba2102", "598a89d4019d99d3db418b3d266249273661edcb", "a03c67d412a2ebc71cb53cf8412ff9a7ab9da1e1", "5ce9f39260dbdebf04128553ac452679480d92f7", "e790cdc1d44d6ce361c21ca573bd490b36ea1ef2", "3b24bd46da070d8593d07c6d24561edaaf289025", "b312309a3cb713fad42e4efc4f084fbdb888d3f6"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "89": {"changesets": [{"author": "Ted Campbell \u003ctcampbell@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056504: Fix spidermonkey make-install for generated files.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nThe 'make install' rule is still used by downstream embedders like GnomeJS so\nfix some bitrot.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313341\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313784\n", "files": ["js/src/build/Makefile.in"], "git_node": "3ac1151a1bf7ca30b6c4992514d03c8d85e79e5b", "git_parents": ["b312309a3cb713fad42e4efc4f084fbdb888d3f6"], "node": "b8ebe18e677a5bb101ae97c33e9d94a1a3c5c4da", "parents": ["f07803e1aa588589f5130a79f43e835614d1d0bc"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785468738, "git_changesets": ["3ac1151a1bf7ca30b6c4992514d03c8d85e79e5b"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "9": {"changesets": [{"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2046483 - enable periodic-update and pinning-update cron jobs on esr153.  a=pascalc\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312545\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312655\n", "files": [".cron.yml"], "git_node": "92cc8624088dff2164f8edbb3a16b6389acc3fa3", "git_parents": ["c754d4f2d60ffacfa3aaab1134fed75ed4c9d3ef"], "node": "d544c9d3d1e5b1b6a7a9462e9033dc9257476322", "parents": ["abd1fe67f4c3b677caecb582d55601a7b1191dc4"], "tags": []}], "date": 1784289908, "git_changesets": ["92cc8624088dff2164f8edbb3a16b6389acc3fa3"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "90": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jonathan Sudiaman \u003cjsudiaman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1931546 - Avoid using stale reference to megalist. r=credential-management-reviewers,dimi a=test-only\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D308640\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/satchel/megalist/content/tests/browser/browser_passwords_filter.js"], "git_node": "cb2f6c0549afe4770378af831e414c96e9439d1a", "git_parents": ["3ac1151a1bf7ca30b6c4992514d03c8d85e79e5b"], "node": "1750e9ddf54c22a61e2b6430564cd697208e7979", "parents": ["b8ebe18e677a5bb101ae97c33e9d94a1a3c5c4da"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emma Zuehlcke \u003cemz@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052897 - Split the ETP customize tests and allow extra time under ChaosMode verify. r=mconley a=test-only\n\nbrowser_etp_customize_2.js exceeded the test-verify timeout, so split its\ntasks across browser_etp_customize_2/3/4.js (cookies, fingerprinting/telemetry,\ntracking protection). Each task must reopen the pane, which renders slowly under\nmacOS ChaosMode, so add requestLongerTimeout to absorb those passes.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310811\n", "files": ["browser/components/preferences/tests/etp/browser-srd.toml", "browser/components/preferences/tests/etp/browser_etp_customize_2.js", "browser/components/preferences/tests/etp/browser_etp_customize_3.js", "browser/components/preferences/tests/etp/browser_etp_customize_4.js"], "git_node": "e7322ac38921f0590e9f4919f59bd9d60880ea40", "git_parents": ["cb2f6c0549afe4770378af831e414c96e9439d1a"], "node": "06eecf8b765d1bc6c7938db51f806f5e02b8f889", "parents": ["1750e9ddf54c22a61e2b6430564cd697208e7979"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Naz\u0131m Can Alt\u0131nova \u003ccanaltinova@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2038445 - Disable GC zeal in profiler/bug2002982.js to fix intermittent failures r=mgaudet a=test-only\n\nThe test expects the number of registered script sources to stay the\nsame across a profiler disable/enable cycle. On sm-compacting builds a\nzeal GC can run between the two enableGeckoProfiling calls and discard\nthe JitScripts of scripts that are no longer on the stack (prologue.js\nand self-hosted), so their sources don't get re-registered on the second\nenable and the counts no longer match. Disable GC zeal at the start of\nthe test to keep it deterministic.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312038\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/profiler/bug2002982.js"], "git_node": "f815328b072efaaca17d1ae7c7c1756cdab9f7a0", "git_parents": ["e7322ac38921f0590e9f4919f59bd9d60880ea40"], "node": "51b4ca0ecb2642a48be9ff1a36d991da8ca36eb8", "parents": ["06eecf8b765d1bc6c7938db51f806f5e02b8f889"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785469014, "git_changesets": ["cb2f6c0549afe4770378af831e414c96e9439d1a", "e7322ac38921f0590e9f4919f59bd9d60880ea40", "f815328b072efaaca17d1ae7c7c1756cdab9f7a0"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "91": {"changesets": [{"author": "Andy Leiserson \u003caleiserson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059531 - Update wgpu to upstream 17d977a9 (2026-07-01)  a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315436\n", "files": [".cargo/config.toml.in", "Cargo.lock", "gfx/wgpu_bindings/Cargo.toml", "gfx/wgpu_bindings/moz.yaml", "supply-chain/audits.toml", "third_party/rust/wgpu-core/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/wgpu-core/src/command/transfer.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-hal/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/wgpu-hal/src/dx12/command.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-hal/src/dx12/mod.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-hal/src/metal/command.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-hal/src/metal/mod.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-hal/src/vulkan/command.rs", "third_party/rust/wgpu-hal/src/vulkan/mod.rs"], "git_node": "974243ee84c54dd16e687d640b04c8d6e724eeb7", "git_parents": ["f815328b072efaaca17d1ae7c7c1756cdab9f7a0"], "node": "c48c15f4e1a88d2ea40ad38ec76749bacaf2a69c", "parents": ["51b4ca0ecb2642a48be9ff1a36d991da8ca36eb8"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785505287, "git_changesets": ["974243ee84c54dd16e687d640b04c8d6e724eeb7"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "92": {"changesets": [{"author": "Thomas Wisniewski \u003ctwisniewski@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2031600 - remove our UA override for indeed.com;  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313770\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/webcompat/data/interventions/2031600-indeed.com.json", "browser/extensions/webcompat/manifest.json"], "git_node": "6098a0b4fa1ee9b9e0a9e3758cd05da754aec9cd", "git_parents": ["974243ee84c54dd16e687d640b04c8d6e724eeb7"], "node": "a984f4df6c3a85678270b5b0215b4f49038b14e7", "parents": ["c48c15f4e1a88d2ea40ad38ec76749bacaf2a69c"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785505452, "git_changesets": ["6098a0b4fa1ee9b9e0a9e3758cd05da754aec9cd"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "93": {"changesets": [{"author": "Rob Wu \u003crob@robwu.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2045676 - Gracefully handle broken files in verifyBundleSignedState  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D305180\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315593\n", "files": ["toolkit/mozapps/extensions/internal/XPIInstall.sys.mjs", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_signed_verify.js"], "git_node": "9d1c688b81535ed51433320c56b34b44d4edf405", "git_parents": ["6098a0b4fa1ee9b9e0a9e3758cd05da754aec9cd"], "node": "dda3c97d9524147d08af1201270260f1d520d610", "parents": ["a984f4df6c3a85678270b5b0215b4f49038b14e7"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785506212, "git_changesets": ["9d1c688b81535ed51433320c56b34b44d4edf405"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "94": {"changesets": [{"author": "Vincent Hilla \u003cvhilla@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2045635 - Validate more fields for nsDocShellLoadState.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D305101\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315218\n", "files": ["docshell/base/nsDocShellLoadState.cpp", "dom/security/nsContentSecurityManager.cpp"], "git_node": "739c55464c1d40b5259ebb813d0e84eacc1114de", "git_parents": ["9d1c688b81535ed51433320c56b34b44d4edf405"], "node": "a3d48abae796569cf1f7a7a6c931f0e38c572359", "parents": ["dda3c97d9524147d08af1201270260f1d520d610"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785506236, "git_changesets": ["739c55464c1d40b5259ebb813d0e84eacc1114de"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "95": {"changesets": [{"author": "Alastor Wu \u003calwu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "[ESR 153] Bug 2045404 - Clean up the Web Speech task lifecycle.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nESR 153 predates bug 2049486, which moved Web Speech media control handling\ninto the content process, so the trunk patch does not apply. On this branch\nMediaSharedKeysListener still lives in nsSpeechTask and holds a raw reference\nto its owning task, while the window's ContentMediaController holds the\nlistener alive through a strong reference. Shutdown() only ran from\nDispatchEndImpl and DispatchErrorImpl, so a task destroyed without an end or\nerror event left a registered listener with a dangling back-reference.\n\nStop media control from ~nsSpeechTask() as a backstop, and factor the\nstart/stop of the listener into helpers so every path goes through the same\ncode.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315502\n", "files": ["dom/media/webspeech/synth/nsSpeechTask.cpp", "dom/media/webspeech/synth/nsSpeechTask.h"], "git_node": "5ef81d3e41a3747d4d6eb221d1f060f55ec54312", "git_parents": ["739c55464c1d40b5259ebb813d0e84eacc1114de"], "node": "3a5d996b8c3dd58ce49e7c425cc08d2a2ad5a069", "parents": ["a3d48abae796569cf1f7a7a6c931f0e38c572359"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785506261, "git_changesets": ["5ef81d3e41a3747d4d6eb221d1f060f55ec54312"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "96": {"changesets": [{"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2033181: Check for active ServiceWorkers  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D295439\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315498\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/HttpChannelParent.cpp"], "git_node": "841e6444f8ffa5dda569fbdb8bd3014ba857f2ef", "git_parents": ["5ef81d3e41a3747d4d6eb221d1f060f55ec54312"], "node": "081dfb5b7074e9884a83b0b1b69690b9a01c0706", "parents": ["3a5d996b8c3dd58ce49e7c425cc08d2a2ad5a069"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785506286, "git_changesets": ["841e6444f8ffa5dda569fbdb8bd3014ba857f2ef"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "97": {"changesets": [{"author": "Tom Schuster \u003ctschuster@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2022253 - Validate principal in BackgroundParentImpl::RecvCreateNotificationParent.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D309842\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315552\n", "files": ["ipc/glue/BackgroundParentImpl.cpp"], "git_node": "c02f02f6406f6167b719da14aa266f8fedd67a61", "git_parents": ["841e6444f8ffa5dda569fbdb8bd3014ba857f2ef"], "node": "4820bc3c88660ba3ec7cd6e8602ffc2acadcbabe", "parents": ["081dfb5b7074e9884a83b0b1b69690b9a01c0706"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785506310, "git_changesets": ["c02f02f6406f6167b719da14aa266f8fedd67a61"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "98": {"changesets": [{"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2045379 - Return nsresult from AudioPacketizer::Input and guard sample-count calculation r=webrtc-reviewers,dbaker a=RyanVM\n\nGuard the sample-count calculation and the buffer grow size with CheckedUint32, and make `AudioPacketizer::Input` return an error otherwise.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D309206\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315479\n", "files": ["dom/media/AudioPacketizer.h", "dom/media/TimedPacketizer.h", "dom/media/gtest/TestAudioPacketizer.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegAudioEncoder.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/MediaEngineWebRTCAudio.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/transportbridge/MediaPipeline.cpp"], "git_node": "abd983ec7513b42b885d1751db474ed5829a4740", "git_parents": ["c02f02f6406f6167b719da14aa266f8fedd67a61"], "node": "a42bb6eef99544fca47620e08763d235a1f1b57c", "parents": ["4820bc3c88660ba3ec7cd6e8602ffc2acadcbabe"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785506336, "git_changesets": ["abd983ec7513b42b885d1751db474ed5829a4740"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "99": {"changesets": [{"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2045379 - Grow the AudioPacketizer buffer with a fallible allocation  a=RyanVM\n\nAllocate the grown buffer fallibly so an allocation failure is surfaced to the caller.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D309886\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315480\n", "files": ["dom/media/AudioPacketizer.h"], "git_node": "30f6ba6ce490fdf0f6a00eefa03eb1d0b1bb57c7", "git_parents": ["abd983ec7513b42b885d1751db474ed5829a4740"], "node": "30b00bbd776627128b5f709772567683ecbe918f", "parents": ["a42bb6eef99544fca47620e08763d235a1f1b57c"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785506604, "git_changesets": ["30f6ba6ce490fdf0f6a00eefa03eb1d0b1bb57c7"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}}
}";